[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3466128459","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112183#issuecomment-3466128459","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112183","id":3466128459,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7OmOxL","user":{"login":"xuhuisheng","id":1118508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTg1MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1118508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xuhuisheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-30T04:55:24Z","updated_at":"2025-10-30T04:55:24Z","body":"## Investigation\n\nWhen there is explicit type declaration, GDScriptAnalyzer will find two candidators, including the local variable's type and current context type. But after the first iteration, `is_base` will always `false`. So next iteration cannot mark member variable from current context type as found.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/07f4c066018314f2957e2892b8ddf55df13097e7/modules/gdscript/gdscript_analyzer.cpp#L4219-L4227\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/07f4c066018314f2957e2892b8ddf55df13097e7/modules/gdscript/gdscript_analyzer.cpp#L4261-L4266\n\nI don't know why we need change `is_base` to `false`. Could I change `is_base` to `true` when `script_class` comes from current context to resolving this issue?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3466128459/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3466972585","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112183#issuecomment-3466972585","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112183","id":3466972585,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Opc2p","user":{"login":"xuhuisheng","id":1118508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTg1MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1118508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xuhuisheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-30T09:40:17Z","updated_at":"2025-10-30T09:40:17Z","body":"After reading relevant PR : https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/70246\n\nI guess the intend of `is_base` is controlling whether we are treating in \"Base Inheritance Class\" or \"Outer class\".\n\n- When \"is_base=true\", we are searching in \"Base Inheritance Class\", we can use `member variable` and `function`\n- When \"is_base=false\", we are searching in \"Outer class\", we cannot use `member variable` and `function`\n\nBut when using implicit type declaration, there is no `Base Inheritance class` part, so \"Outer class\" are used by `is_base=true`, accidentally. So I want to ask whether the \"cannot find identity\" is expected?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3466972585/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]